  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.2. Increased capacity of Member States to ensure safe and healthy working conditions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2022, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development established the National Council for Occupational Safety and Health, headed by the Minister of Human Resources and Social Development, with membership of representatives of a number of relevant government agencies, and representatives of employers and workers.
The establishment of this council stems from the objectives of the National Transformation Programme to keep pace with Vision 2030 and the labour market strategy to achieve the comprehensive national vision in the field of occupational safety and health, as this is one of the main priorities that Saudi Arabia seeks to achieve.
Among the most prominent tasks of the National Council for Occupational Safety and Health are the following: reviewing legislation, regulations, and programs related to occupational safety and health, developing a comprehensive national program for reporting accidents and injuries at work and related diseases, documenting reports and results of investigations, and developing capacities and resources in the field of occupational safety and health. Other roles and tasks include: developing and governing occupational safety and health at the national level, establishing an effective and comprehensive monitoring and evaluation system for occupational safety and health, reviewing periodic reports related to occupational safety and health, and enhancing cooperation between employers, workers and their representatives to promote occupational safety and health. With the support from the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, the ILO provided technical inputs on the role and functions of the National Occupational Safety and Health Council. ILO also provided technical advice on the composition and mandates of the council, in particular in the importance of tripartite representatives in the council.</narrative>
   </description>
